[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-27638"] :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-103289/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c39ea976-b5f9-5004-a552-68c5c025132b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103289/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b08c447a-cc1d-58c7-87af-7e3ac3d32a74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103289/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "749bbc90-2eb3-5bf8-94a4-e98f5302c1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103289/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "961ce003-6035-5a1f-9aa6-141fd94606dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103289/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "44e70e67-040e-58ec-8e2b-2215930016dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103289/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3944d1c-16bd-589e-b90e-443fdf8f4cd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103289/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-103289/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-103289/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-103289/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-103289/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-103289/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103289" :question/id #uuid "264dc1d8-6c35-583a-b855-2ee23edf3c8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103289" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $\n- The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/732955302ca49a41f6c43cf242d7c869e630e88d804c4b56a5beb3b081f2d230.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere, except where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-103289/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103289"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-28675/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "99e13b58-77bb-5f71-afc8-21d1feaa855f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28675/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6a83dd0b-504f-5ddd-b816-f900a2db858a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28675/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "134ed3a0-8b4e-57f7-b6d8-9846c0144eb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28675/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "57c8061b-6304-50f4-8639-49df6546865a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28675/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0f3efb74-8a3d-5cad-82a2-9d3e8b0b8d89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28675/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e838b5c5-420a-5bb5-ae26-c4d18b43ae16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-28675/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-28675/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-28675/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-28675/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-28675/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-28675/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-28675" :question/id #uuid "a50a54b2-642a-5810-b035-b477949523f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-28675" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).$\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi $\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x)=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-28675/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-28675"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-29608/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e313fd4f-5890-5bfc-bdb5-c0c87715a5d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29608/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "187883db-7955-5ba8-acd5-afc1c014a35b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29608/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b17045a2-633d-548c-bcae-239dc7f561a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29608/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "a052a079-715a-50a6-810b-0672caede357" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29608/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2ddfd7ce-95fd-515f-b2e3-7163e700eb36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-29608/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "31b8fc33-67bf-512c-a450-8f06bb931f2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-29608/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-29608/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-29608/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-29608/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-29608/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-29608/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-29608" :question/id #uuid "22cad6db-7a8e-526c-ae29-9691aa02e418" :question/math-academy-id "q-29608" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n- $tan⁡(x)=tan⁡(x+2n\\pi ).$\n- The range of the function is $[-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+2n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi +n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )=tan⁡(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=tan⁡x$ is $(-\\infty ,+\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-29608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-29608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103295/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "6adf4eaa-a986-5f83-911e-4759f7bd183f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103295/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6e945b93-d364-508a-92fa-2823a1c5dbe4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103295/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "22d203ee-ab5a-5dfb-8879-4e89e5cf102d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103295/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3ab27600-9377-5b2b-a4b4-dc6697afd59c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103295/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e88fdd70-1af2-5d17-af59-4f2afd8ef738" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103295/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8979ad8-23a5-583c-b1b2-f6796537e051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103295/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-103295/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-103295/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-103295/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-103295/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-103295/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103295" :question/id #uuid "317d2b9c-f42d-5ece-9543-51e9cfb75b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103295" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The vertical asymptotes of the function are $x=2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,0)$\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933873/assets/c2d0606829588b01f6cba2fa4785b201c47a6d9ffa325d54e64544c9769d7e4a.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,0).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :q